            <div xml:id="d39">

                <pb facs="0183" n="71" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg71"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 21158.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé of Austria-Hungary to the Secretary of
                        State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Austro-Hungarian Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Manchester, Mass.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1909-08-18"><hi rendition="#italic">August 18,
                        1909</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2028.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Your Excellency</hi>: Rudolf Warren-Lippit, residing
                    and owning property at Thurnisch, Rann Parish, Steiermark, Austria, claims to be
                    an American citizen and is also in possession of a passport issued by the former
                    United States Legation at Vienna, No. 104, and dated December 31, 1879.</p>
                <p>The Austro-Hungarian ministry of foreign affairs has instructed me to ascertain
                    whether Mr. Rudolf Warren-Lippit, as well as his son of the same name, born in
                    1890 at Thurnisch, Steiermark, are really American citizens.</p>
                <p>I therefore have the honor to request your excellency to kindly have this
                    information procured, and permit myself to await an answer in due course.</p>
                <p>Please accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">L. Ambrózy.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
